# TTS Audio — Current Source of Truth

The implementation in `scripts/generate-tts.ts` and `npm run tts:audit` is
authoritative. Content authors fix pronunciation through content fields, not by
editing the script.

## Commands

Use full lesson IDs for A2/B1/B2:

```powershell
npm run tts:audit -- --lesson b2-lesson-01
npm run tts:generate -- --lesson b2-lesson-01 --model gemini
npm run tts:audit -- --lesson b2-lesson-01
npm run check:audio
```

A1 numeric shorthand remains valid:

```powershell
npm run tts:generate -- --lesson 04 --model gemini
```

`tts:audit` is read-only: no API calls, directories, MP3 writes or deletes. It
reports expected jobs, existing/missing files, model/voice counts, unsupported
types, risky spoken text and coverage gaps. Add `--verbose` to list each job.

## Gemini models

### Gemini 2.5 Flash TTS

Default for isolated lexical/grammar material:

- `content.vocabulary`;
- image labels and flags;
- reading flip-card words;
- `audio_choice` words;
- grammar table rows/notes;
- grammar highlights;
- grammar visual tiles without a connected description;
- A2 wide cards.

### Gemini 2.5 Pro TTS

Default for connected speech:

- dialogues;
- reading paragraphs and optional full reading;
- listening;
- table-fill paragraphs;
- personal-choice models;
- grammar examples (unless the exercise explicitly requests Flash);
- illustrated cards/phrases (unless a card explicitly requests Flash);
- grammar visual tiles with a description;
- illustrated-card header captions.

Very short Pro clips can truncate; isolated difficult words may still sound
better with Pro. Content overrides decide exceptional cases.

Chirp is a Philip-only fallback, not the normal lesson workflow.

## Override priority

Prefer fields beside the content:

1. Spoken text:
   - `ttsText`
   - `ttsLabel`
   - `ttsParagraphs`
   - `ttsNotes`
   - `exampleTtsTexts`
2. Model: `ttsModel: 'flash' | 'pro'` or an exercise-level `ttsFlash/ttsPro`.
3. Prompt: `ttsPrompt`.
4. Legacy script ID maps exist only for A1/A2 backward compatibility.

Alex must not add B1/B2 IDs to script-level maps.

## Dialogue voices — stable by character

Available Gemini voices:

- female primary: Achernar;
- female secondary: Despina;
- male primary: Charon;
- male secondary: Achird.

Assignment is per dialogue section:

1. `speaker` is the stable character identity.
2. First female character → Achernar; second → Despina.
3. First male character → Charon; second → Achird.
4. The same `speaker` keeps the same voice across all turns.
5. Unnamed two-person legacy dialogues use stable even/odd turns.
6. More than two same-gender characters share the primary voice and produce an
   audit warning.

Always provide `speaker` and `voiceGender` when the textbook identifies a
character. Do not alternate voices merely because two consecutive lines have
the same gender.

## What the main generator collects

- vocabulary → `words/{id}.mp3`
- illustrated/grouped cards → `words/{card.id}.mp3`
- illustrated-card caption → `texts/{exerciseId}-caption.mp3`
- image labels / flags / audio-choice words → `words/*.mp3`
- dialogues → `dialogues/{exerciseId}-{sectionId}-line-{index}.mp3`
- grammar visual/table/examples/highlight → `grammar/*.mp3`
- reading/table-fill paragraphs → `texts/{exerciseId}-p-{index}.mp3`
- eligible full reading → `texts/{exerciseId}-full.mp3`
- listening → `listening/{exerciseId}.mp3`
- personal choice model → `texts/{exerciseId}-model.mp3`

The generator respects `disableAudio`, `disableTts` and grammar-row `noAudio`.
B1/B2 multi-panel grammar rows use the same flattened index as the UI.

If a custom B2 component calls `getTtsAudioPath()` but audit reports
`unsupported-b2-audio-type`, stop and ask Philip to add a collector.

## Preflight before first generation

Content must be reviewed/frozen first.

Check:

- every dialogue line: `speaker`, `voiceGender`, numbers/abbreviations;
- numbers, years, times, prices and measurements use spoken words in TTS fields;
- `=` and `/` are replaced with natural pauses/words in spoken text;
- abbreviations (`НДК`, `жк`, `бул.`, `ул.`, `г.`) are expanded;
- `ttsParagraphs.length === paragraphs.length`;
- `paragraphVoiceGenders.length === paragraphs.length` when present;
- `ttsNotes.length === notes.length` when present;
- custom exercise types have collected jobs.

Run audit. Fix errors before generation; review warnings instead of blindly
suppressing them.

## Numbers and abbreviations

Display text may keep digits. Spoken text should use natural Bulgarian:

```ts
{
  text: 'Билетът е 5,50 евро.',
  ttsText: 'Билетът е пет евро и петдесет евроцента.',
}
```

Reading:

```ts
paragraphs: ['Паркът е създаден през 1882 г.'],
ttsParagraphs: ['Паркът е създаден през хиляда осемстотин осемдесет и втора година.'],
```

Do not put raw `=`, `/`, table separators or grammar abbreviations into spoken
text. Use periods/commas for clear pauses.

## Regeneration

The generator skips existing files. For a correction:

1. Identify the exact affected MP3 from audit/component path.
2. Fix the content override.
3. Delete only that MP3 (or the smallest exact pattern).
4. Run the lesson generator again.
5. Audit + `check:audio`.
6. Human-listen to the affected clip in the browser.

Never delete a whole lesson audio folder for one bad word.

## Human listening remains required

Audit cannot judge stress, emotion, pacing or whether a homograph sounds
natural. Listen at minimum to:

- every dialogue section;
- every long reading/listening text;
- client-reported problem words;
- grammar rows with numbers/symbols;
- clips using custom prompts/models.

## Git

- MP3 files are ordinary Git blobs, never Git LFS.
- Commit content first.
- Commit reviewed audio separately.
- `npm run check:audio` must pass before audio push.
